WEBVTT

00:00:07.000 --> 00:00:10.100
In science class, we're studying different animals.

00:00:11.066 --> 00:00:13.199
There was a lesson about baby animals.

00:00:13.933 --> 00:00:15.833
Here are some interesting ones.

00:00:17.566 --> 00:00:19.666
Look at this kangaroo!

00:00:20.033 --> 00:00:21.999
I think he goes to the gym!

00:00:23.033 --> 00:00:26.899
It's difficult to believe he was a little baby once.

00:00:27.700 --> 00:00:29.333
How about these toads?

00:00:29.766 --> 00:00:34.266
Once upon a time, they were little babies called tadpoles.

00:00:35.233 --> 00:00:37.933
There weren't any baby butterflies to see

00:00:37.933 --> 00:00:41.099
because they start out as these caterpillars!

00:00:42.200 --> 00:00:46.433
Or how about this adult flamingo? He's pink!

00:00:46.433 --> 00:00:48.533
But he wasn't pink as a baby.

00:00:49.066 --> 00:00:54.366
Oh no, he was grey. His parents weren't worried about that.

00:00:54.366 --> 00:01:00.232
All baby flamingos are grey! There were cute baby animals, too.

00:01:00.700 --> 00:01:03.600
Like this tapir from South America.

00:01:04.333 --> 00:01:10.033
But in my opinion, there wasn't a cuter baby animal than this seal.

00:01:12.000 --> 00:01:14.700
That's all for today! Bye!

00:01:18.700 --> 00:01:21.066
Which language does the vlogger use? We use <i>was/were</i>

00:01:25.533 --> 00:01:31.199
We use <i>was/were</i> to talk about how people or things were before now.

00:01:31.966 --> 00:01:34.199
He was a little baby once.

00:01:34.700 --> 00:01:38.033
They were little babies called tadpoles.

00:01:40.433 --> 00:01:45.566
We use <i>there was/there were</i> to talk about situations in the past.

00:01:46.800 --> 00:01:52.100
There was a lesson about baby animals. There were cute baby animals, too.

00:01:56.233 --> 00:02:01.533
The negative past tense of the verb <i>to be</i> is <i>wasn't/weren't</i>

00:02:01.533 --> 00:02:05.699
But he wasn't pink as a baby. His parents weren't worried about that.

00:02:09.033 --> 00:02:12.733
There wasn't a cuter baby animal than this seal.

00:02:12.733 --> 00:02:14.733
There weren't any baby butterflies.

00:02:22.300 --> 00:02:23.033
<b>Use it!</b>

00:02:24.666 --> 00:02:27.599
Use the pictures and words to make sentences.

00:02:39.533 --> 00:02:41.266
<i><b>There was</b> an eagle.</i>

00:02:42.100 --> 00:02:43.666
<i><b>There wasn't</b> a parrot.</i>

00:02:43.666 --> 00:02:44.532
Now you try.

00:02:54.833 --> 00:02:56.333
<i><b>There wasn't</b> a monkey.</i>

00:02:57.400 --> 00:02:58.600
<i><b>There was</b> a mouse.</i>

00:03:09.600 --> 00:03:11.600
<i><b>There weren't</b> any giraffes on the farm.</i>

00:03:12.333 --> 00:03:13.599
<i><b>There were</b> horses.</i>

00:03:24.666 --> 00:03:27.266
<i><b>There were</b> lions at the wildlife centre.</i>

00:03:27.266 --> 00:03:28.866
<i><b>There weren't</b> any bears.</i>